    "result_text": "The test tree contains only the acceptance test (the other two files are helpers). The build compiled everything (regenerating `OwnerDto` from the updated openapi spec) and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133):\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Removed `getMembershipTier()` (which returned `GOLD`/`SILVER`/`BRONZE`) and added `getMembershipLevel()` returning an `Integer`: starts at 1, `+1` when an email is present, `+1` when `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3 (with a note that level 4 is reserved for tenure).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` string property in the `OwnerDto` schema with a `membershipLevel` integer (int32, min 1, max 3, read-only). MapStruct maps it by name from the entity getter, and the DTO is regenerated from this spec at build time \u2014 so the response now exposes `membershipLevel` instead of `membershipTier`.\n\nOn the audit line: the spec noted \"anything that recorded the tier (such as the create audit line) must record the level instead,\" but in this codebase the create audit line (`owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026`) never recorded the tier, so there was nothing to convert \u2014 I left it unchanged rather than adding an unrequested field. The response was the only thing that carried the tier.\n\n**Result:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**. The acceptance test `coreNumericLevel` (unique owner with email \u2192 `$.membershipLevel == 3`) passes.\n\nNote: the `householdSize` field (previously only used to derive the old `GOLD` tier) is still populated on creation but no longer consumed. I left it in place to keep the change minimal and avoid touching persistence; let me know if you'd like it removed.",
